  "reason": "Evidence: The best configuration so far is config_024 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, concat) at 0.629 acc. The largest gains came from multiprofile (+9.4 pts over singleprofile) and avgpool aggregation (+3 pts over transformer). However, the RNA encoder has only been tested as pca_n2000 across all experiments, and RNA is the dominant signal (0.485 RNA-only vs ~0.21-0.23 image-only). Question: Does a learned, biologically-informed RNA representation (scvi_n200) improve over PCA in the best-performing multimodal multiprofile architecture? Why this is the best next experiment: It sits in the most promising region of the search space (multiprofile + avgpool + concat + ViT-L), directly tests the single most impactful unexplored variable (RNA encoder quality), and has the highest potential to yield a direct improvement on our current best. If scvi_n200 helps, we gain a concrete upgrade; if it does not, we confirm PCA sufficiency and can redirect effort toward image-side or fusion refinements. This is a high-information, high-leverage test under the limited budget."
}

